        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://shawneehillsoh.org/community/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Original lots measured 35 by 70 feet, and early streets were built without public water or sewer because utilities were unavailable.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://shawneehillsoh.org/community/history",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 2001 the village had about 419 residents, 200 homes, and 30 businesses, reflecting its slow early growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://shawneehillsoh.org/community/history",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "census_demographic"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Delaware County grew 64.3% from 1990 to 2000, the fastest growth rate in Ohio during that decade.",
